      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the number of divisors of the number $24$, we can use the prime factorization method. \n\nFirst, let's find the prime factorization of $24$:\n\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nTo find the number of divisors, we use the formula that involves the exponents of the prime factors. If a number $n$ has a prime factorization of the form $p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\ldots \\times p_k^{e_k}$, then the number of divisors of $n$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nIn the case of $24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1$, the exponents are $3$ and $1$. Applying the formula:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of $24$ is $\\boxed{8}$.",
