      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number \\(24\\), we start by performing its prime factorization. The prime factorization of \\(24\\) is:\n\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of positive divisors of a number \\(n\\) with the prime factorization \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor the number \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), we have \\(e_1 = 3\\) and \\(e_2 = 1\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of \\(24\\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).\n\nTo verify, we list all the positive divisors of \\(24\\):\n\\[\n1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24\n\\]\n\nThere are indeed \\(8\\) divisors. Hence, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
