      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of a given number, we can use the prime factorization of the number. The number 24 can be factored into its prime components as follows:\n\n\\[ 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\]\n\nThe formula to calculate the number of positive divisors of a number is derived from its prime factorization. If \\( n \\) has the prime factorization \\( p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\ldots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\), then the number of positive divisors \\( d(n) \\) is given by:\n\n\\[ d(n) = (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\]\n\nFor \\( n = 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\):\n\n\\[ e_1 = 3 \\text{ and } e_2 = 1 \\]\n\nThus, the number of positive divisors is:\n\n\\[ d(24) = (3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of positive divisors of 24 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
